# OS
.DS_Store

# Runtime data the app writes. All of it normally lives under XDG directories
# (~/.local/share/local-edit, ~/.cache/local-edit), so these entries are
# purely defensive — for anyone who runs with XDG_* pointed at the checkout.
#
# These MUST stay anchored with a leading slash, and this project has two traps
# that make the rule sharper than usual:
#
#   * An unanchored "bin/" would also match bin/local-edit — the launcher
#     wrapper the .desktop file execs. The repo would clone and not run. That
#     matters more here than it did there: this project's engine is `sd-cli`
#     plus twenty .so files, so the temptation to ignore a whole directory is
#     correspondingly stronger.
#   * An unanchored "models/" is the obvious thing to want ignored for the
#     downloaded weights, and would keep matching if a source directory were
#     ever given that name.
#
# The soundboard project shipped exactly this bug (commit 82e6270, "Anchor
# runtime ignores so they stop excluding soundboard/library/") and produced a
# repository that could not import itself. Do not repeat it.
/models/
/engine/
/bin/sd-cli
/bin/sd-server
/bin/*.so
/bin/*.so.*
/work/
/out/
/samples/
/tmp/
settings.json
*.log

# Test and benchmark artifacts
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
